===Mainnet PLONK example with external verifier (mode = 1)===

A PLONK end-to-end test was performed on Dogecoin mainnet using the same broadcast driver (<code>contrib/zk_carrier/scripts/broadcast_set.sh</code>) with <code>PROOF_SYSTEM=plonk</code>. TX_C and TX_R were broadcast sequentially (without waiting for confirmation between them) and were both accepted by mainnet:

<pre>
TX_C: fd48360fe39c11f769300cf4700482a1fbefe17df7a625fd571bdb869a809d36 → block 6190360 (2026-05-02 21:02:02 UTC, fee 2000000)
TX_R: 6308399a614a2163dad32d92e4fe3973f1897d28c4c6ca0c8ebf76a0b31f53d7 → block 6190369 (2026-05-02 21:12:57 UTC, fee 20000000)
commit32:    fb603dfdef91452a163f6497f0fa1da8f10c5b051552959eb036a363ddb48fce
payload_len: 2285 bytes (ZKP1 mode=1 PLONK; embedded public.json + proof.json)
Reveal explorer: https://chain.so/tx/DOGE/6308399a614a2163dad32d92e4fe3973f1897d28c4c6ca0c8ebf76a0b31f53d7
</pre>

After confirmation, the canonical external verifier (<code>snarkjs plonk verify</code>) was invoked end-to-end against the same <code>verification_key_plonk.json</code> committed under <code>contrib/zk_carrier/circuits/build/</code> and the <code>proof.json</code> / <code>public.json</code> that were embedded as the on-chain ZKP1 reveal payload:

<pre>
External verifier (PLONK) — invoked end-to-end after mainnet reveal confirmed
  vkey:          contrib/zk_carrier/circuits/build/verification_key_plonk.json
  vkey_sha256:   7051f9fe4719f9f12ceaec46c7be778425c674b93b07f3eaf903a4cb7a6db8c4
  proof_sha256:  b10a78e887642e262e79f204b85cda5f8c3deda6c206793459a19bb366578a5d
  public_sha256: 8f44ff43fd8fa80fbf3f36e38ade7abd23a4be288ac8997326503cd93cadced0

+ snarkjs plonk verify verification_key_plonk.json public.json proof.json
[INFO]  snarkJS: PLONK VERIFIER STARTED
[INFO]  snarkJS: OK!
rc=0
</pre>

This validates the documented split: spvnode enforces the on-chain commitment binding, and the external verifier — invoked AFTER the reveal lands and is matched — enforces the cryptographic proof check.

A recent mainnet checkpoint is baked in at height 6189700 (hash <code>a6ed6d6b03668d0bb9baddfbc52565b2514d02f118d6d0298a6ca48d511d7804</code>, 2026-05-02T09:18:05Z) so <code>spvnode -p</code> rescans of these and subsequent ZK carrier pairs only need to sync the final ~200–300 blocks of headers before reaching the published commitments.

==Deployment==

Phase 1 can be deployed immediately in wallets, tooling, and SPV infrastructure without consensus change.

Phase 2 requires a separate consensus-track proposal and activation plan, ideally co-sequenced with the PQC carrier's Phase 2 to share an OP_SUCCESSx allocation block.

